    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense hinges on the elite projection of **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88), who stands as our clear anchor against Hancock today. Despite facing a slightly above-average arm, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and a favorable batting order position that vaults his daily outlook into the \"Strong\" category. While **Jackson Merrill** (60.98) also cracks the 60-point threshold, he faces a trickier test against Abbott; however, his top-of-the-order role provides enough volume to maintain his status as an essential start. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (56.35) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (56.78) fall just short of the 60-point \"Strong\" tier, primarily due to the elite quality of opposing arms like S\u00e1nchez and Webb, but their situational platoon advantages keep them as high-upside plays for Roto production.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal production floor at the bottom of the order, specifically regarding **Nasim Nunez** (39.32). While **Nasim Nunez** is a high-priority asset for our pursuit of SB category dominance, his sub-40 efficiency score\u2014dragged down by a poor projected spot in the lineup\u2014necessitated a benching to preserve game caps. He narrowly missed the cut over **Curtis Mead** (45.04), as the optimizer favored the latter\u2019s superior platoon matchup and higher spot in the batting order to capture counting stats. With **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining sidelined on the IL and **Kyle Tucker** unavailable due to the schedule, we are operating with a condensed core; we must continue to monitor **Coby Mayo** (48.28), whose utility remains strictly situational given his current placement in the back of the order and the diminishing returns of his current platoon split.",
